WEBVTT

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:05.220
Is that right?

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:07.930
So Raetsel is making her way there now.

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:11.960
Understood. Keep a close eye on her.

00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:21.180
This wound up taking quite some time.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:24.930
But it should be over before much longer,

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:26.250
Lovushka.

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:30.770
Soon our puzzle of vengeance 
will come to an end...

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:43.520
What did you need to tell us, Principal?

00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:47.750
Yeah! Why’d ya randomly 
summon us to the boonies?

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:52.350
Did you find some clues 
leading to Raetsel and Jin?

00:00:57.170 --> 00:01:01.620
This island used to be the home 
for a POG training institute.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.370
Are you tellin’ us that

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:07.440
you and Jin have trained here on this island?

00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:09.130
That’s right.

00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:10.830
That grave...

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:15.370
By any chance, did you and 
Jin-Jin lose a friend here...?

00:01:17.650 --> 00:01:20.510
She was Jin’s rival.

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:21.510
Jin’s...?!

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:27.020
She was a Solver who loved 
puzzles and died for them.

00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:30.070
Lovushka...

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:06.040
I Want to Make a World with Full Bellies

00:03:13.850 --> 00:03:18.050
I’ve heard that deciphering ancient 
script can be akin to solving a puzzle.

00:03:18.890 --> 00:03:20.740
If we could just discern the key principle...

00:03:24.820 --> 00:03:26.060
Are you thinking about Kaito?

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:30.310
It still... isn’t over yet.

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:33.910
The Book of God, the Puzzle of God...

00:03:33.910 --> 00:03:36.180
Not to mention the Armlet of Orpheus.

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:39.290
Is the principal going to tell Kaito?

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:40.320
I imagine he will.

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:49.380
It’s yet another sad story 
created by the Puzzle of God...

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:51.580
Lovushka?

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:57.310
Upon graduating from Root Gakuen, 
Jin and I entered the POG.

00:03:57.930 --> 00:04:01.060
That is where we met her.

00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:13.480
What is it, Jin?

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:17.220
Thank you for the meal! I appreciate it!

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:20.410
Welp, now that I have a full belly...

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:29.620
Nice!

00:04:30.170 --> 00:04:31.560
5.68 seconds?!

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:33.000
Wow!

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:37.680
I see! You must be Lovushka.

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:39.700
I’m sorry, but who might you be?

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:41.760
How do you know my name?

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:45.980
I heard that one other Solver had joined...

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:48.070
As expected, she’s good!

00:04:48.070 --> 00:04:51.070
Yeah, she scored around the same time as you.

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:52.490
The same time?

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:56.880
Ah, then does that mean you’re Jin Makata?!

00:04:57.200 --> 00:04:59.370
And that’d make you Baron Kaidou?!

00:05:00.450 --> 00:05:02.540
How did you know it was us?

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:05.130
I heard that we just got an incredible new

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:07.130
Solver along with his Giver partner!

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:10.030
I’m Lovushka! It’s nice to meet you.

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:12.010
Yeah, the pleasure’s mine.

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:14.300
Nice to meet you!

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:18.170
It’s a pleasure!

00:05:20.930 --> 00:05:25.670
Just like Jin, she was one of 
the few Solvers in the POG.

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:28.250
In which case, that woman...

00:05:28.690 --> 00:05:32.090
Yeah. She was one of the Phi-Brain 
candidates hand-selected

00:05:32.090 --> 00:05:34.100
by Count Pythagoras.

00:05:34.780 --> 00:05:36.390
But back then,

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:39.830
we were still oblivious of the 
Count’s devious schemes.

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:45.570
When it came to puzzles, Jin 
was one step ahead of her.

00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:48.950
Between Jin having to run 
to keep ahead of Lovushka

00:05:49.460 --> 00:05:51.830
and Lovushka running to catch up to Jin,

00:05:52.650 --> 00:05:54.580
the two pushed each other to greater heights.

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:57.330
They grew to become wonderful rivals.

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:06.090
You sure love those things!

00:06:06.650 --> 00:06:10.980
I never had it until I came here, 
but rice really is good, isn’t it?

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:14.900
Salty rice balls! Just 
salt and rice! How simple!

00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:16.600
Okay, I get it!

00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:20.520
You see, my homeland is so poor

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:23.360
that I never got to eat good food like this.

00:06:26.750 --> 00:06:30.110
The only toys I ever had 
were some handmade puzzles.

00:06:32.090 --> 00:06:32.960
I see...

00:06:33.550 --> 00:06:35.840
You know, I’ve got a dream!

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:36.620
A dream?

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:41.580
I will assist the Count, 
solve the Puzzle of God and

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:43.000
obtain the Book of God.

00:06:44.560 --> 00:06:46.970
All because I want to make 
a world with full bellies.

00:06:47.810 --> 00:06:49.540
A world with full bellies?

00:06:50.060 --> 00:06:54.070
Yep! Everyone will get to eat 
yummy food until they’re full.

00:06:54.990 --> 00:06:56.270
That’s the type of world I want.

00:06:58.110 --> 00:07:00.520
Yeah? That’s a good dream.

00:07:02.120 --> 00:07:06.030
Plus, I wanna try ALL the delicious 
food this world has to offer.

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:09.200
How about you? What’s your dream, Jin?

00:07:10.040 --> 00:07:12.460
Me? Mine’s pretty obvious!

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:16.260
It’s to become a Phi-Brain 
and solve the Puzzle of God.

00:07:16.260 --> 00:07:18.260
And what will you do after that?

00:07:18.260 --> 00:07:20.160
After that? What do you mean?

00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:22.670
If you get the Book of God, isn’t there

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:24.920
something you’d like to ask for in return?

00:07:25.520 --> 00:07:26.460
Not really.

00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:31.300
Isn’t the Puzzle of God the 
hardest puzzle in the world?

00:07:31.940 --> 00:07:33.930
I’ve just gotta solve it!

00:07:34.230 --> 00:07:35.360
Puzzle-loving idiot.

00:07:35.990 --> 00:07:37.680
You’re not one to talk!

00:07:39.150 --> 00:07:42.270
“Just gotta solve it,” 
huh? That’s so you, Jin!

00:07:45.950 --> 00:07:47.170
Thank you for the meal!

00:07:48.620 --> 00:07:49.520
I appreciate it.

00:07:50.290 --> 00:07:52.450
But your dream won’t come true.

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:56.080
I’m the one who will become the Phi-Brain!

00:07:57.460 --> 00:07:58.580
I’ll take that as a challenge!

00:08:07.430 --> 00:08:13.860
However, with the passage of time, 
the gap in their abilities only grew.

00:08:14.980 --> 00:08:20.530
Lovushka was unable to keep up 
with Jin’s remarkable progress.

00:08:20.820 --> 00:08:21.850
And then...

00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:28.220
Jin!

00:08:30.410 --> 00:08:33.280
Is that the Armlet of Orpheus?

00:08:34.040 --> 00:08:35.780
You actually got it!

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:40.290
Yeah! This brings me one step 
closer to becoming a Phi-Brain.

00:08:40.930 --> 00:08:43.890
The journey’s still long and 
I haven’t admitted defeat yet!

00:08:44.220 --> 00:08:45.300
Yeah!

00:08:46.760 --> 00:08:52.970
But then Jin saw a future where Count 
Pythagoras destroyed the world.

00:08:54.810 --> 00:08:57.340
You know what happened from there...

00:08:57.860 --> 00:09:00.220
And what became of Miss Lovushka?

00:09:01.110 --> 00:09:04.160
I’ve heard that when she 
found out Jin went missing,

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:06.730
she took the news very hard.

00:09:07.370 --> 00:09:09.230
No! Jin’s missing...?

00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:11.510
That can’t be true...

00:09:13.790 --> 00:09:18.000
After that, she began challenging 
the Puzzles of Fools.

00:09:28.060 --> 00:09:29.000
Dead?!

00:09:29.770 --> 00:09:30.920
Lovushka’s dead?!

00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:38.370
I’ve been told she lost her 
life in a Puzzle of Fools.

00:09:42.530 --> 00:09:44.280
Why did she push herself so hard?

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:46.770
It was to become a Phi-Brain, huh?

00:09:47.530 --> 00:09:49.300
A world with full bellies...

00:09:49.700 --> 00:09:52.670
I bet all she wanted was to 
make her dream come true...

00:09:53.210 --> 00:09:55.110
I wonder if that’s truly 
all there was to it.

00:09:56.500 --> 00:09:58.210
Lovu-Lovu was a good girl,

00:09:59.170 --> 00:10:03.220
but her dream may have gotten 
twisted somewhere along the line...

00:10:04.510 --> 00:10:06.660
Her dream got twisted?

00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:10.040
So why are you telling all of this to us?

00:10:10.430 --> 00:10:15.350
Yeah. You’ve got a bad habit of 
draggin’ out the prelude, Principal.

00:10:15.810 --> 00:10:17.930
The prelude? That was the prelude?

00:10:18.560 --> 00:10:20.150
The meat of the story’s coming up.

00:10:20.690 --> 00:10:23.930
I have no idea where this is 
going, but let’s hear it!

00:10:24.530 --> 00:10:27.180
Miss Lovushka just so 
happened to have a fiancé.

00:10:27.780 --> 00:10:29.240
Upperclassman Jikukawa?!

00:10:29.240 --> 00:10:30.440
You’re tellin’ the story?!

00:10:31.330 --> 00:10:35.710
He was a childhood friend from the 
same country as Miss Lovushka.

00:10:36.330 --> 00:10:40.450
Supposedly he had been making 
puzzles as her personal Giver.

00:10:41.460 --> 00:10:46.800
After Lovushka died, I caught word 
that he perished in a car accident.

00:10:47.820 --> 00:10:49.080
But he survived the accident!

00:10:50.300 --> 00:10:52.520
He made it look as though 
he died in the accident,

00:10:52.520 --> 00:10:56.170
erased his own existence and began 
a new life as a different person.

00:10:56.170 --> 00:10:58.090
Why would he do that?

00:10:58.940 --> 00:11:01.470
Around the time Miss Lovushka died,

00:11:01.470 --> 00:11:03.910
her motherland began mining rare metals,

00:11:03.910 --> 00:11:06.600
which created sudden economic growth.

00:11:07.530 --> 00:11:09.710
He took advantage of the chaos to sneak into

00:11:09.710 --> 00:11:11.600
the heart of the country’s government.

00:11:11.950 --> 00:11:14.250
Eventually, he climbed 
his way to the very top.

00:11:14.580 --> 00:11:15.610
The top?

00:11:16.250 --> 00:11:17.860
No way! Is he...?!

00:11:18.830 --> 00:11:22.870
Lovushka and this man were both 
from the Republic of Amgine!

00:11:29.260 --> 00:11:30.120
Enigma!

00:11:30.970 --> 00:11:31.790
No...

00:11:33.180 --> 00:11:34.540
Zagadka...

00:11:35.390 --> 00:11:38.110
Correct. I am Zagadka.

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:43.320
And Lovushka was the love of my life...

00:11:53.990 --> 00:11:56.650
Enigma, what are you doing here?!

00:11:57.660 --> 00:12:01.650
I noticed you were snooping 
into my affairs yet again.

00:12:02.380 --> 00:12:05.280
Remember what I said? I 
won’t keep any secrets.

00:12:05.840 --> 00:12:08.410
It would seem I’ve made a pest of myself.

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:10.120
I’m sorry.

00:12:13.180 --> 00:12:15.680
So you figured it out after all, Baron?

00:12:15.680 --> 00:12:18.800
Amgine is a nation that tightly 
controls all information.

00:12:19.890 --> 00:12:22.650
Although the corroborative 
investigation didn’t run smoothly,

00:12:22.650 --> 00:12:24.680
Mr. Jikukawa did a splendid job.

00:12:25.190 --> 00:12:27.180
This photograph is what served 
as our conclusive evidence.

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:29.680
If you zoom in...

00:12:32.530 --> 00:12:34.190
Isn’t that some sort of scar?

00:12:34.950 --> 00:12:38.670
Zagadka had an old scar 
in the exact same spot.

00:12:39.290 --> 00:12:40.870
I heard that when he was young,

00:12:40.870 --> 00:12:43.780
he got it by protecting Lovushka 
from some falling rocks.

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:50.450
The two of us had relied on each other to 
survive in our poor, barren motherland.

00:12:50.930 --> 00:12:52.640
How could I bring myself to get it removed?

00:12:53.970 --> 00:12:56.720
Even though you were willing 
to change your face and name,

00:12:56.720 --> 00:13:00.640
you were unable to erase the 
bonds you shared with her.

00:13:01.640 --> 00:13:03.470
So everything was part of one big lie?

00:13:05.860 --> 00:13:08.470
Including how you said Jin hated puzzlers?

00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:12.620
And how he asked you to 
gather up the Master Brains?

00:13:12.620 --> 00:13:13.450
Everything?!

00:13:14.070 --> 00:13:15.730
Yeah, those were all lies.

00:13:17.660 --> 00:13:18.480
What the hell?!

00:13:19.080 --> 00:13:20.480
Was this all for Lovushka?

00:13:20.750 --> 00:13:21.910
Huh?

00:13:21.910 --> 00:13:25.500
Are you avenging Lovushka 
since a puzzle took her life?

00:13:26.210 --> 00:13:29.550
Yes, this is all for Lovushka.

00:13:30.210 --> 00:13:34.680
Becoming the President and 
destroying all of the puzzlers...

00:13:34.680 --> 00:13:36.470
Everything I’m doing has been for Lovushka!

00:13:36.890 --> 00:13:40.000
But didn’t Miss Lovushka love puzzles?

00:13:40.310 --> 00:13:43.050
There is no way she’d be happy 
if she saw what you’re doing!

00:13:43.230 --> 00:13:44.010
Shut up!

00:13:46.060 --> 00:13:49.480
How could you children possibly 
understand how Lovushka felt?

00:13:50.320 --> 00:13:54.320
You have no idea how much agony 
those puzzles put Lovushka through!

00:14:00.290 --> 00:14:02.020
Aren’t you going to eat, Lovushka?

00:14:03.710 --> 00:14:05.400
Hey, Zagadka...

00:14:06.080 --> 00:14:06.900
What is it?

00:14:07.840 --> 00:14:14.660
I... To be honest, I’m thinking 
about giving up puzzles.

00:14:15.130 --> 00:14:15.860
What?

00:14:16.970 --> 00:14:21.390
Jin’s been chosen by the 
Armlet, but I haven’t...

00:14:22.350 --> 00:14:26.170
The more I work with puzzles, the more 
I see that I’m falling behind Jin.

00:14:29.480 --> 00:14:31.530
He’s not like me, not Jin...

00:14:32.690 --> 00:14:35.110
He has something that I lack!

00:14:36.160 --> 00:14:40.690
I... I don’t have it. 
I’m missing something...

00:14:41.490 --> 00:14:42.920
That’s not true!

00:14:43.250 --> 00:14:46.070
There is no way your dream 
could lose to that man!

00:14:46.750 --> 00:14:49.070
Let’s keep at it, Lovushka!

00:15:00.140 --> 00:15:02.580
I assume you’ve heard the 
news regarding Jin Makata.

00:15:03.060 --> 00:15:03.750
I have.

00:15:04.310 --> 00:15:06.610
He is working to obtain the Book of God

00:15:06.610 --> 00:15:09.620
so that he may bring his 
ambitions to fruition.

00:15:10.400 --> 00:15:13.150
No! Jin isn’t that type of person!

00:15:13.150 --> 00:15:15.490
Then why did he go into hiding?

00:15:15.690 --> 00:15:16.780
Well...

00:15:18.110 --> 00:15:20.350
Your dream will never come true.

00:15:21.990 --> 00:15:25.120
If he beats you to the Book of God,

00:15:25.250 --> 00:15:29.080
you will be unable save your 
motherland or your loved ones.

00:15:30.290 --> 00:15:32.150
Become a Phi-Brain!

00:15:32.840 --> 00:15:36.370
Become a Phi-Brain before Jin Makata does!

00:15:38.880 --> 00:15:40.730
Let’s go for it, Lovushka!

00:15:41.140 --> 00:15:41.870
But...

00:15:42.390 --> 00:15:45.150
If Jin steals the Book of God, your--

00:15:45.700 --> 00:15:47.630
our dream will be over.

00:15:50.810 --> 00:15:53.650
I hold your dream of the utmost importance!

00:15:54.230 --> 00:15:56.390
I’ll do whatever I can 
to make it come true.

00:15:57.640 --> 00:15:58.890
Zagadka...

00:15:59.820 --> 00:16:04.330
Let’s protect our dream--our 
shared puzzle--Lovushka!

00:16:25.930 --> 00:16:26.980
Lovushka!

00:16:37.070 --> 00:16:39.900
You need to eat some! This isn’t healthy.

00:16:42.160 --> 00:16:43.780
Don’t lose heart!

00:16:44.330 --> 00:16:45.370
It’ll work out.

00:16:45.860 --> 00:16:47.900
Knowing you, I’m sure 
you’ll become a Phi-Brain.

00:16:48.830 --> 00:16:49.640
Let’s keep at it!

00:16:50.290 --> 00:16:53.790
A world... with full... bellies...

00:16:54.250 --> 00:16:57.910
A world... with full... bellies...

00:17:00.590 --> 00:17:02.400
You can do it, Lovushka!

00:17:13.850 --> 00:17:14.960
Lovushka?

00:17:15.810 --> 00:17:16.930
Lovushka!

00:17:24.320 --> 00:17:26.940
She can’t be... No!

00:17:28.290 --> 00:17:31.230
Lovushka!

00:17:38.300 --> 00:17:39.750
I know the truth now.

00:17:40.220 --> 00:17:43.130
The Count had merely been using Lovushka.

00:17:44.470 --> 00:17:46.710
Her dream got twisted...

00:17:47.300 --> 00:17:50.520
Aren’t you doing the exact 
frigging thing to Raetsel?!

00:17:51.270 --> 00:17:53.590
The Count used Lovushka.

00:17:54.270 --> 00:17:55.840
And you’re using Raetsel.

00:17:56.480 --> 00:17:59.400
And here Amgine became a wealthy country...

00:17:59.690 --> 00:18:03.750
Lovu-Lovu never got to 
see the people she loved

00:18:03.750 --> 00:18:05.350
become happy, did she?

00:18:06.200 --> 00:18:10.860
That is precisely why I made her 
dream come true in her stead!

00:18:12.540 --> 00:18:16.900
I have built Amgine into the 
type of country she dreamt of.

00:18:16.900 --> 00:18:17.990
That doesn’t make sense.

00:18:19.300 --> 00:18:22.660
Amgine began developing due 
to the rare metals just

00:18:22.660 --> 00:18:25.290
before Miss Lovushka passed away!

00:18:25.290 --> 00:18:27.800
Then you didn’t have anything 
to do with its growth!

00:18:28.550 --> 00:18:31.160
So that means even if Miss 
Lovushka didn’t push

00:18:31.160 --> 00:18:33.210
herself to solve all those puzzles...

00:18:33.810 --> 00:18:36.320
Don’t tell me... You never told her?

00:18:37.150 --> 00:18:39.980
You were aware of your 
homeland’s imminent boom,

00:18:40.480 --> 00:18:42.320
but didn’t inform her.

00:18:43.320 --> 00:18:46.030
That’s preposterous! Why 
didn’t you tell her?!

00:18:46.410 --> 00:18:48.970
Lovushka was going to save our country.

00:18:49.370 --> 00:18:52.150
Allowing someone to beat her to it...

00:18:52.790 --> 00:18:55.280
That was NOT an option!

00:18:56.370 --> 00:18:57.690
That’s horrible!

00:18:57.690 --> 00:19:01.030
It was you! You’re the one who killed her!

00:19:01.670 --> 00:19:03.000
It was the puzzles!

00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:05.210
The puzzles were to blame for everything!

00:19:05.840 --> 00:19:09.290
Zagadka, you’re the one who 
drove Lovushka to her death!

00:19:09.600 --> 00:19:12.020
You killed her with your own two hands!

00:19:12.930 --> 00:19:14.170
Mr. Principal...

00:19:14.810 --> 00:19:19.360
If puzzles didn’t exist, 
Lovushka never would have died.

00:19:19.360 --> 00:19:22.230
The Count never would have 
been blinded by ambition!

00:19:23.480 --> 00:19:25.010
Wh-what’s wrong with him?

00:19:25.650 --> 00:19:29.110
He’s taking the sadness of having 
lost his fiancé out on puzzles.

00:19:29.570 --> 00:19:32.030
He’s blaming puzzles for everything...

00:19:32.490 --> 00:19:34.400
He’s got some nasty resentment problems!

00:19:34.700 --> 00:19:36.090
Kaito Daimon!

00:19:37.250 --> 00:19:39.630
Your parents never would have died!

00:19:39.750 --> 00:19:42.230
Rook and the other Phi-Brain children never

00:19:42.230 --> 00:19:44.760
would have endured such cruel fates!

00:19:44.760 --> 00:19:49.300
The Orpheus Order wouldn’t have 
been manipulated by Klondike!

00:19:49.300 --> 00:19:52.500
Puzzles! Puzzles are to blame for everything!

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:53.930
Shut up!

00:19:56.640 --> 00:19:58.420
The puzzles didn’t do anything wrong.

00:20:00.270 --> 00:20:02.420
There isn’t a single puzzle that was born

00:20:02.420 --> 00:20:05.900
with the desire to hurt 
someone or take lives!

00:20:06.650 --> 00:20:09.610
The problem... is with 
the people who made them!

00:20:11.490 --> 00:20:15.970
If you... If you’re a Giver, 
then can’t you hear them?

00:20:15.970 --> 00:20:17.750
Can’t you hear the puzzles’ cries?!

00:20:28.420 --> 00:20:30.050
I can’t believe it...

00:20:30.470 --> 00:20:36.210
After all they’ve put you through, 
you still believe in puzzles.

00:20:36.560 --> 00:20:39.100
You’re a fool beyond repair.

00:20:39.100 --> 00:20:40.350
What?!

00:20:40.350 --> 00:20:44.310
But that is what makes extending 
this invitation worth my while.

00:20:44.650 --> 00:20:45.870
What invitation?

00:20:53.990 --> 00:20:55.600
Wait, Zagadka!

00:20:55.910 --> 00:20:59.110
Raetsel is waiting for 
you in Hell’s Valley.

00:20:59.700 --> 00:21:01.040
Hell’s Valley?

00:21:01.750 --> 00:21:05.220
She’s waiting to face you 
in one last puzzle battle.

00:21:05.930 --> 00:21:07.370
It’s a trap, Kaito!

00:21:07.920 --> 00:21:11.300
After coming this far, 
I won’t set any traps!

00:21:11.930 --> 00:21:14.420
It doesn’t matter to 
me one way or the other.

00:21:15.010 --> 00:21:18.150
I don’t care if you win or if Raetsel wins!

00:21:18.530 --> 00:21:19.380
What?!

00:21:19.850 --> 00:21:22.880
Regardless of who wins, one 
of you is destined to die.

00:21:23.350 --> 00:21:25.610
Admittedly, it would be ideal 
if you destroyed each other,

00:21:25.610 --> 00:21:27.890
ending with both of you meeting 
your respective deaths.

00:21:28.730 --> 00:21:32.130
Solve this puzzle, Kaito Daimon!

00:21:41.120 --> 00:21:43.290
Kaito Daimon is on his way here?

00:21:43.290 --> 00:21:47.590
Yeah. Apparently the POG managed 
to pinpoint your location.

00:21:47.590 --> 00:21:49.240
What are you going to do, Raetsel?

00:21:49.800 --> 00:21:52.130
I’m done with running and hiding.

00:21:52.630 --> 00:21:54.540
This is where I’ll defeat Kaito Daimon!

00:21:56.760 --> 00:21:58.600
Doesn’t she sound reliable?

00:21:59.220 --> 00:22:02.550
She’s no longer a kitten. 
She’s a fierce wildcat.

00:22:03.270 --> 00:22:05.650
Now let’s move out, Lovushka.

00:22:06.110 --> 00:22:10.610
It’s time to complete the puzzle we shared.

00:22:13.740 --> 00:22:15.940
I won’t let anyone take Jin.

00:22:16.700 --> 00:22:17.530
Raetsel...

00:22:18.770 --> 00:22:19.830
Fight.

00:22:20.450 --> 00:22:25.320
Put your soul--all of your 
passion--into that puzzle.

00:24:03.260 --> 00:24:05.270
I had noticed the truth all along...

00:24:05.270 --> 00:24:07.850
There never was a Jin who 
hated puzzles and transpired

00:24:07.850 --> 00:24:09.480
to destroy all of the puzzlers...

00:24:09.480 --> 00:24:15.900
Even so--No, that’s 
why I went on a journey.

00:24:16.440 --> 00:24:17.680
I’m going to tell you.

00:24:17.680 --> 00:24:21.100
This is the real reason why 
I went on a journey with Jin.

00:24:21.160 --> 00:24:27.980
The Journey Ends

00:24:21.370 --> 00:24:23.060
Next time, “The Journey Ends.”

00:24:23.660 --> 00:24:25.330
I won’t let you have Jin.

00:24:25.330 --> 00:24:27.040
Puzzle time, start!

00:24:27.980 --> 00:24:30.990
Fin Art: Akeru Otsuki
